 {"sec": "Approach — physical examination · p235", "page": 235, "q": "Petechiae or purpura in a child with anaemia indicates —", "opts": ["Vitamin K deficiency only", "Thrombocytopenia", "Platelet dysfunction with normal count", "Vascular fragility alone"], "ans": 1, "exp": "The heading 'petechiae/purpura (thrombocytopenia)' lists leukaemia, aplastic anaemia and HUS. (Book p235)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-037"},
 {"sec": "Approach — physical examination · p235", "page": 235, "q": "Which of the following causes thrombocytopenia with a notably acute onset?", "opts": ["Leukaemia", "Iron deficiency anaemia", "Haemolytic uraemic syndrome", "Aplastic anaemia"], "ans": 2, "exp": "HUS is specifically annotated as having an acute onset. (Book p235)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-038"},
 {"sec": "Approach — physical examination · p235", "page": 235, "q": "Splenomegaly in a child with anaemia points to ___.", "opts": ["Iron deficiency anaemia", "Anaemia of chronic inflammation", "Acute blood loss", "Haemolytic anaemia"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Splenomegaly → haemolytic anaemia. (Book p235)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-039"},
 {"sec": "Approach — physical examination · p235", "page": 235, "q": "Splenomegaly with hepatomegaly or generalised lymphadenopathy in an anaemic child suggests —", "opts": ["Leukaemia", "Hereditary spherocytosis", "Thalassaemia trait", "Megaloblastic anaemia"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Splenomegaly a/w hepatomegaly → leukaemia; generalised lymphadenopathy → leukaemia. (Book p235)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-040"},
 {"sec": "Approach — physical examination · p235", "page": 235, "q": "Match the physical finding with its likely cause:", "opts": ["A-1, B-3, C-4, D-2", "A-4, B-3, C-1, D-2", "A-3, B-4, C-2, D-1", "A-4, B-2, C-3, D-1"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Correct pairs: Absent radius/thumb→Fanconi anaemia with bone marrow failure; Petechiae/purpura→Thrombocytopenia (leukaemia, aplastic anaemia, HUS); Splenomegaly→Haemolytic anaemia; Hepatosplenomegaly→Leukaemia. (Book p235)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Absent radius/thumb", "Haemolytic anaemia"], ["Petechiae/purpura", "Leukaemia"], ["Splenomegaly", "Thrombocytopenia (leukaemia, aplastic anaemia, HUS)"], ["Hepatosplenomegaly", "Fanconi anaemia with bone marrow failure"]], "id": "PEDS-C50-041"},
 {"sec": "Approach — physical examination · p235", "page": 235, "q": "A 3-year-old has pallor, generalised lymphadenopathy, hepatosplenomegaly and petechiae.", "opts": ["Iron deficiency anaemia", "Haemolytic uraemic syndrome", "Leukaemia", "Hereditary spherocytosis"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Pallor with lymphadenopathy, hepatosplenomegaly and thrombocytopenic petechiae points to leukaemia. (Book p235)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 3-year-old has pallor, generalised lymphadenopathy, hepatosplenomegaly and petechiae over the limbs.", "id": "PEDS-C50-042"},
 {"sec": "Approach — physical examination · p235", "page": 235, "q": "True or False — An absent thumb in a child with anaemia should raise the suspicion of Fanconi anaemia.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — skeletal defects such as absent radius/thumb are seen in Fanconi anaemia with bone marrow failure. (Book p235)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C50-043"},
 {"sec": "Approach — physical examination · p235", "page": 235, "q": "Odd one out (conditions causing petechiae/purpura with anaemia):", "opts": ["Hereditary spherocytosis", "Leukaemia", "Aplastic anaemia", "Haemolytic uraemic syndrome"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Hereditary spherocytosis is not in the thrombocytopenia list; the other three are. (Book p235)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C50-044"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "Based on MCV, a low MCV indicates ___ anaemia.", "opts": ["Dimorphic", "Microcytic", "Normocytic", "Macrocytic"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Low MCV → microcytic anaemia. (Book p235)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-045"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "Which is the most common cause of microcytic anaemia in children?", "opts": ["Anaemia of chronic disease", "Sideroblastic anaemia", "Iron deficiency anaemia", "Thalassaemia"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Low MCV causes: iron deficiency anaemia (m/c), ACD/ACI, thalassaemia. (Book p235)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-046"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "High MCV on the haemogram indicates ___ anaemia.", "opts": ["Microcytic", "Normocytic", "Haemolytic", "Macrocytic"], "ans": 3, "exp": "High MCV → macrocytic anaemia; normal MCV → normocytic anaemia. (Book p235)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-047"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "Match the MCV category with the corresponding anaemia:", "opts": ["A-3, B-1, C-4, D-2", "A-1, B-3, C-2, D-4", "A-4, B-3, C-1, D-2", "A-4, B-1, C-3, D-2"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Correct pairs: Low MCV→Microcytic anaemia; Normal MCV→Normocytic anaemia; High MCV→Macrocytic anaemia; Iron deficiency→Microcytic hypochromic picture. (Book p235)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Low MCV", "Normocytic anaemia"], ["Normal MCV", "Microcytic hypochromic picture"], ["High MCV", "Microcytic anaemia"], ["Iron deficiency", "Macrocytic anaemia"]], "id": "PEDS-C50-048"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "In the low-MCV algorithm, the first step when there is a history/finding suggestive of IDA is —", "opts": ["Hb electrophoresis", "Trial of therapeutic iron", "Serum ferritin", "Bone marrow examination"], "ans": 1, "exp": "History/findings suggestive of IDA → yes → trial of therapeutic iron → assess response. (Book p235)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-049"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "In the low-MCV algorithm, if the response to a trial of therapeutic iron is positive, the child is —", "opts": ["Evaluated for thalassaemia", "Sent for marrow biopsy", "Treated as IDA", "Subjected to serum ferritin testing"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Response (+) → treat as IDA; response (−) → serum ferritin. (Book p235)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-050"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "In the low-MCV algorithm with no response to iron, a low serum ferritin indicates ___.", "opts": ["Thalassaemia", "ACD/ACI", "Sideroblastic anaemia", "IDA"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Serum ferritin: low → IDA; normal → thalassaemia; high → ACD/ACI. (Book p235)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-051"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "In the low-MCV algorithm with no response to iron, a normal serum ferritin indicates ___.", "opts": ["Thalassaemia", "IDA", "ACD/ACI", "Lead poisoning"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Normal ferritin after an iron-unresponsive microcytic anaemia indicates thalassaemia. (Book p235)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-052"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "In the low-MCV algorithm with no response to iron, a high serum ferritin indicates ___.", "opts": ["Haemolytic anaemia", "ACD/ACI", "IDA", "Thalassaemia"], "ans": 1, "exp": "High ferritin → anaemia of chronic disease/inflammation. (Book p235)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-053"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "Serum ferritin in iron deficiency anaemia is used as a ___ test.", "opts": ["Therapeutic monitoring of compliance", "Genetic", "Screening", "Confirmatory biopsy"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Low serum ferritin is described as the screening test in the IDA blood parameters. (Book p237)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-054"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "The normal reticulocyte count is ___.", "opts": ["0.1–0.5%", "3–5%", "5–10%", "1–2%"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Reticulocyte count normal: 1–2%; it indicates bone marrow response. (Book p235)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-055"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "The reticulocyte count in anaemia indicates —", "opts": ["Bone marrow response", "Body iron stores", "Folate stores", "Degree of haemolysis directly"], "ans": 0, "exp": "The reticulocyte count indicates bone marrow response. (Book p235)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-056"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "Corrected reticulocyte count = reticulocyte count × patient's Hb ÷ normal Hb for age and gender, with the normal Hb taken as —", "opts": ["13", "15", "11", "12"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Corrected reticulocyte count uses normal Hb for age/gender (taken as 15). (Book p235)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-057"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "A corrected reticulocyte count that indicates adequate bone marrow response is more than ___.", "opts": ["0.5%", "5%", "2%", "1%"], "ans": 2, "exp": "> 2% indicates adequate bone marrow response. (Book p235)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-058"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "A corrected reticulocyte count below 2% in a normocytic anaemia means —", "opts": ["Adequate marrow response", "Immediate indication for transfusion", "Pathognomonic of haemolysis", "An inadequate marrow response needing further evaluation"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Low corrected reticulocyte count (< 2%) means inadequate marrow response and directs the algorithm further. (Book p235)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-059"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "An 18-month-old has Hb 8 g/dl, MCV 62 fl and a normal examination; he does not respond to 4 weeks of oral iron.", "opts": ["Check serum ferritin — a normal value indicates thalassaemia", "Repeat the iron trial for 3 more months", "Start vitamin B12 injections", "Transfuse packed cells"], "ans": 0, "exp": "In the low-MCV algorithm, an iron-unresponsive child proceeds to serum ferritin: low = IDA, normal = thalassaemia, high = ACD/ACI. (Book p235)", "type": "case", "stem": "An 18-month-old has Hb 8 g/dl and MCV 62 fl with a normal examination; there is no rise in haemoglobin after 4 weeks of supervised oral iron.", "id": "PEDS-C50-060"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 235, "q": "True or False — A reticulocyte count above 2% indicates an adequate bone marrow response.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — > 2% (corrected) indicates adequate marrow response. (Book p235)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C50-061"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "Which set of tests constitutes the evidence of haemolysis?", "opts": ["Hb electrophoresis, HPLC, G6PD assay", "Reticulocyte count alone", "Peripheral smear, LDH, bilirubin and haptoglobin", "Ferritin, TIBC, transferrin saturation"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Evidence of haemolysis: peripheral smear (+), ↑ LDH, ↑ bilirubin, ↓ haptoglobin. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-062"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "In haemolysis, haptoglobin is —", "opts": ["Increased", "Normal", "Absent only in intravascular haemolysis", "Decreased"], "ans": 3, "exp": "↓ haptoglobin is part of the evidence of haemolysis. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-063"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "A low corrected reticulocyte count with no evidence of haemolysis and normal WBC and platelet counts indicates —", "opts": ["Pure red cell aplasia", "Aplastic anaemia", "Megaloblastic anaemia", "Acute blood loss"], "ans": 0, "exp": "No haemolysis + normal WBC/platelets → pure red cell aplasia (Diamond-Blackfan syndrome). (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-064"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "A low corrected reticulocyte count with pancytopenia points to —", "opts": ["Acute blood loss", "Bone marrow failure", "Pure red cell aplasia", "Autoimmune haemolysis"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Pancytopenia → bone marrow failure: aplastic anaemia, megaloblastic anaemia. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-065"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "Haemolytic anaemia secondary to aplastic crisis is caused by —", "opts": ["Cytomegalovirus", "Hepatitis A", "Parvovirus B19", "Epstein-Barr virus"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Haemolytic anaemia d/t aplastic crisis (Parvovirus B19) or autoimmune haemolytic anaemia. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-066"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "A high corrected reticulocyte count ( > 2%) without evidence of haemolysis indicates —", "opts": ["Aplastic crisis", "Autoimmune haemolysis", "Diamond-Blackfan syndrome", "Acute blood loss"], "ans": 3, "exp": "In the algorithm, haemolysis (−) with a high reticulocyte count → acute blood loss. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-067"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "A high corrected reticulocyte count with positive haemolysis evidence directs to —", "opts": ["Haemolytic anaemia", "Bone marrow biopsy", "Iron therapy trial", "Serum ferritin"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Haemolysis (+) with high reticulocyte count → haemolytic anaemia → evaluate. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-068"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "A 6-year-old with pallor has a corrected reticulocyte count of 6%, positive peripheral smear for haemolysis, ↑ LDH and ↓ haptoglobin.", "opts": ["Acute blood loss", "Haemolytic anaemia", "Pure red cell aplasia", "Aplastic anaemia"], "ans": 1, "exp": "High corrected reticulocyte count with haemolysis evidence → haemolytic anaemia → evaluate (e.g. aplastic crisis from parvovirus B19 or autoimmune haemolysis). (Book p236)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 6-year-old with pallor has a corrected reticulocyte count of 6%, spherocytes on the peripheral smear, LDH 900 U/L, indirect bilirubin 3 mg/dl and low haptoglobin.", "id": "PEDS-C50-069"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "True or False — In the low-MCV algorithm, a high serum ferritin in an iron-unresponsive child indicates thalassaemia.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — high ferritin = ACD/ACI; NORMAL ferritin = thalassaemia. (Book p235)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C50-070"},
 {"sec": "Investigations and algorithms · p235–236", "page": 236, "q": "Odd one out (evidence of haemolysis):", "opts": ["Raised LDH", "Raised bilirubin", "Positive peripheral smear", "Raised haptoglobin"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Haemolysis LOWERS haptoglobin; the other three rise. (Book p236)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C50-071"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "IDA is the most common cause of anaemia in children ___.", "opts": ["Worldwide", "In India only", "In developed countries only", "Above 5 years of age"], "ans": 0, "exp": "IDA is the m/c cause of anaemia in children worldwide. (Book p236)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-072"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "The pathogenesis of IDA is a fall in total body iron stores, reflected by low ___.", "opts": ["TIBC", "Serum ferritin", "Serum transferrin", "Serum iron only"], "ans": 1, "exp": "↓ total body iron stores (↓ serum ferritin) → ↓ erythropoiesis → anaemia. (Book p236)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-073"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "In IDA, reduced erythropoiesis follows a fall in body iron stores; the stores fall only after a few months of —", "opts": ["Chronic infection", "Malabsorption of folate", "Markedly reduced dietary intake", "Acute blood loss"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Note: iron stores ↓ only after a few months of ↓↓ dietary intake. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-074"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "Which pregnancy or early-life factor delays the onset of IDA in infants?", "opts": ["Early introduction of cow milk", "Exclusive breastfeeding beyond 2 years", "Early deworming", "Good iron stores acquired from the mother in utero"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Onset at 9–24 months is LATE d/t good iron stores acquired from the mother in utero. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-075"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "Growth spurts that increase iron demand occur at 0–2 years and ___.", "opts": ["Puberty", "School age", "Infancy only", "Senescence"], "ans": 0, "exp": "↑ demand during growth spurts: 0–2 years and puberty. (Book p236)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-076"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "Malabsorption as a predisposing factor for IDA is exemplified by ___.", "opts": ["Vegan diet", "Celiac disease", "Hookworm infestation", "Puberty growth spurt"], "ans": 1, "exp": "↓ absorption: malabsorption (e.g. celiac disease); ↑ blood loss: worm infestation (hookworm). (Book p236)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-077"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "The worm infestation named as a cause of increased blood loss in IDA is ___.", "opts": ["Enterobius", "Trichuris", "Hookworm", "Ascaris"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Worm infestation, e.g. hookworm, causes increased blood loss. (Book p236)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-078"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "Match the predisposing factor for IDA with its mechanism:", "opts": ["A-4, B-1, C-3, D-2", "A-4, B-1, C-2, D-3", "A-3, B-2, C-1, D-4", "A-2, B-3, C-4, D-1"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Correct pairs: Decreased intake→↓ Dietary iron; Increased demand→Growth spurts at 0–2 years and puberty; Decreased absorption→Malabsorption such as celiac disease; Increased blood loss→Hookworm infestation. (Book p236)", "type": "match", "pairs": [["Decreased intake", "Hookworm infestation"], ["Increased demand", "↓ Dietary iron"], ["Decreased absorption", "Growth spurts at 0–2 years and puberty"], ["Increased blood loss", "Malabsorption such as celiac disease"]], "id": "PEDS-C50-079"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "Atransferrinemia causes iron deficiency anaemia because of defective —", "opts": ["Iron transfer to marrow precursors", "Dietary iron absorption", "Hepatic iron storage", "Hepcidin regulation"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Rare cause: atransferrinemia — iron transfer to red cell precursors in bone marrow. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-080"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "Which is a rare cause of iron deficiency anaemia?", "opts": ["Pubertal growth spurt", "Transferrin receptor antibodies", "Hookworm infestation", "Celac disease malabsorption"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Rare causes of IDA: atransferrinemia and transferrin receptor antibodies. (Book p236)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-081"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "A 20-month-old has Hb 7.8 g/dl, MCV 60 fl and low ferritin; he was exclusively breastfed until 18 months with no iron supplementation.", "opts": ["Anaemia of chronic inflammation", "Diamond-Blackfan syndrome", "Iron deficiency anaemia", "Thalassaemia major"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Low MCV with low ferritin at 9–24 months from inadequate dietary iron = IDA, the m/c anaemia of childhood. (Book p236)", "type": "case", "stem": "A 20-month-old has Hb 7.8 g/dl and MCV 60 fl with low serum ferritin; he was exclusively breastfed until 18 months without iron supplementation.", "id": "PEDS-C50-082"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "True or False — Iron stores fall almost immediately after a single day of poor dietary iron intake.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 1, "exp": "False — iron stores fall only after a few months of markedly reduced dietary intake. (Book p236)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C50-083"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "True or False — Growth spurts at 0–2 years and puberty predispose to iron deficiency by increasing demand.", "opts": ["True", "False"], "ans": 0, "exp": "True — ↑ demand in growth spurts at 0–2 years and puberty is a listed predisposing factor. (Book p236)", "type": "tf", "id": "PEDS-C50-084"},
 {"sec": "IDA pathogenesis and risk factors · p236", "page": 236, "q": "Odd one out (mechanisms predisposing to iron deficiency anaemia):", "opts": ["Hookworm infestation", "Increased renal loss of iron", "Decreased dietary intake", "Increased demand in growth spurts"], "ans": 1, "exp": "The four listed mechanisms are decreased intake, ↑ demand, ↓ absorption and ↑ blood loss; renal iron loss is not described. (Book p236)", "type": "odd", "id": "PEDS-C50-085"},
 {"sec": "IDA features, investigations and treatment · p237", "page": 237, "q": "The most reliable sign of iron deficiency anaemia is —", "opts": ["Glossitis", "Splenomegaly", "Pallor", "Koilonychia"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Most reliable sign: pallor (oral mucosa, nail beds, palpebral conjunctiva). (Book p237)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-086"},
 {"sec": "IDA features, investigations and treatment · p237", "page": 237, "q": "The sites examined for pallor in IDA include the oral mucosa, nail beds and ___.", "opts": ["Sclerae", "Palm creases", "Tympanic membrane", "Palpebral conjunctiva"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Pallor is assessed at the oral mucosa, nail beds and palpebral conjunctiva. (Book p237)", "type": "fill", "id": "PEDS-C50-087"},
 {"sec": "IDA features, investigations and treatment · p237", "page": 237, "q": "Koilonychia means —", "opts": ["Spooning of nails", "Flat nails", "Pitting of nails", "Transverse ridging of nails"], "ans": 0, "exp": "Koilonychia = spooning of nails (platynychia = flat nails). (Book p237)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-088"},
 {"sec": "IDA features, investigations and treatment · p237", "page": 237, "q": "Atrophic glossitis in IDA gives the tongue a ___ appearance.", "opts": ["Geographic with ulcers", "Shiny, smooth", "Beefy red with fissures", "Coated white"], "ans": 1, "exp": "Atrophic glossitis: shiny, smooth tongue (a beefy red tongue belongs to megaloblastic anaemia). (Book p237)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-089"},
