 {"sec": "IDA features, investigations and treatment · p237", "page": 237, "q": "The blood parameter described as the screening test for IDA is —", "opts": ["TIBC", "Marrow iron stain", "Serum ferritin", "Transferrin saturation"], "ans": 2, "exp": "Blood parameters: low MCV and low serum ferritin (screening). (Book p237)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-094"},
 {"sec": "IDA features, investigations and treatment · p237", "page": 237, "q": "The most effective and economical form of iron for treating IDA is —", "opts": ["Ferric ammonium citrate", "Iron dextran injection", "Carbonyl iron", "Ferrous sulphate"], "ans": 3, "exp": "Ferrous sulphate is the most effective & economical form of iron, with 20% elemental iron. (Book p237)", "type": "mcq", "id": "PEDS-C50-095"},
